Thread::Construct keeps the upstream DuplicateHandle over WitOS context capabilities, with the unchanged
INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE fallback; stack-discovery failure terminates the native component. Both HijackReturnAddress
entries hold a native walk scope through every original-stack pointer use. GcScanRoots keeps the upstream
enumeration inside a kernel stack lease: a foreign target is suspended after the runtime rendezvous, and the lease
is released before the paired resume; failure terminates the component.

